# goIRL — portable selkies bundle

Version: __VERSION__ (amd64, Debian 12 ABI)

## Layout
- `selkies-gstreamer-run`  — executable launcher (matches the upstream name)
- `venv/`                  — bundled Python virtualenv with selkies + deps
- `VERSION`                — version string

## Install (matches goirl_gcloud/ansible expectation)

```
sudo install -d -o debian -g debian /opt/selkies
sudo tar -xzf selkies-gstreamer-portable-v__VERSION___amd64.tar.gz \
    -C /opt/selkies --strip-components=1
sudo chown -R debian:debian /opt/selkies
```

The Ansible playbook in `goirl_gcloud` already wires the systemd unit and
runtime flags around this layout.

## Required system packages

This bundle ships the Python side only; the host must already provide the
X11 / GStreamer / PipeWire stack the playbook installs (see
`addons/example/Dockerfile` in the source tree for the exhaustive list).
